    {
      "kind": "explain",
      "title": "Faire can mean ‘to go’",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "text": "Faire does not always mean ‘to do’ or ‘to make’. With some activities it means ‘to go’."
        },
        {
          "t": "cards",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "faire une promenade",
              "sub": "to go for a walk"
            },
            {
              "title": "faire les magasins",
              "sub": "to go shopping"
            },
            {
              "title": "faire un voyage",
              "sub": "to go on a trip"
            },
            {
              "title": "faire une promenade en bateau",
              "sub": "to go for a boat ride",
              "emoji": "🚢"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "callout",
          "text": "‘Faire les magasins’ is shopping for fun. ‘Faire les courses’ is food shopping."
        },
        {
          "t": "reveal",
          "label": "A funny one: faire le pont",
          "text": "Faire le pont literally means ‘to make the bridge’, but it is used for ‘to have a long weekend’. In France, when a bank holiday falls on a Tuesday or a Thursday, people like to ‘faire le pont’."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "explain",
      "title": "Weather and visits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "text": "We also use faire to talk about the weather."
        },
        {
          "t": "cards",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "faire beau",
              "sub": "to be nice weather"
            },
            {
              "title": "faire mauvais",
              "sub": "to be bad weather"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "text": "To say ‘visit’ for a town or city, use faire une visite de + the town or city."
        },
        {
          "t": "list",
          "items": [
            "faire une visite de Paris = to visit Paris",
            "faire une visite de Londres = to visit London",
            "Je fais une visite de Manchester. = I am visiting Manchester."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "callout",
          "text": "Some names of cities sound different in French!"
        }
      ]
    },
